---
description: Keep RockServer HTTP transport modules small and cohesive
alwaysApply: true
---

# HTTP module boundaries

- Do not add handlers, DTOs, or transport helpers to an unrelated HTTP module.
- Place new routes in a domain module (`account`, `pairing`, `catalog`, `voice`) and keep router
  assembly as a thin composition layer.
- When a touched HTTP file mixes more than one domain or becomes difficult to navigate, extract
  the changed domain in the same task before adding more behavior.
- Before handoff, run formatting, lint, tests, and review touched modules for duplication,
  misplaced responsibilities, and dead code. Refactor clear issues within the task scope.
